{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792310585,"nonce":"ZuD0zV3e2Dl/E1vSJTFBQExNHJA=","title":"WORKAROUND APPLIED: `Tensor.fromArray(floats, F32)` in nue/loader/GGUFLoader.hx was resolving bare `F32` to `nue.loader.MetaValue.F32` (a ...","message":"**Workaround landed:** `nue/loader/GGUFLoader.hx:180` now uses `DType.F32` (fully qualified) instead of bare `F32`. llama-chat no longer SIGSEGVs in the forward pass — it now OOM-kills (SIGKILL/137) because the 1B model dequant'd to F32 ≈ 4 GB doesn't fit, but the inference path actually executes and produces token output. 128/128 haxe regression + tiny-transformer + 709 lib tests still green.\n\n**Underlying compiler bug remains:** bare enum-variant resolution doesn't consider expected param type. When two imported scopes define the same variant name (DType.F32 unboxed-ord-0 vs MetaValue.F32 boxed-tag-8), the compiler picks the first match found rather than the one that satisfies the call signature.\n\n\n1. Suspected iface-to-iface dispatch — wrong. Traced through resetCache(slot3), forwardIds(slot2), LlamaModel→blocks[0].forward→TransformerBlock.forward→RMSNorm.forward — all dispatched correctly.\n2. Found Tensor.mul returning NULL because weight had dtype=16/160/240 — pointer-low-byte garbage.\n3. Suspected cross-file MIR lowering of DType — added `[fromArray]` runtime diag, confirmed `dtype=0x9a92cc0e0 dtype_u8=224` in llama-chat vs `dtype=0x0 dtype_u8=0` in tiny-transformer.\n4. **Ruled out tier-up:** `--preset embedded` (no tier promotion, interpreter-only) still showed identical garbage. Same MIR runs everywhere; tier doesn't matter.\n5. Added `[enum-var]` diag in `hir_to_mir.rs` EnumVariant arm (line 8485). Revealed: `mod=nue.loader parent=nue.loader.MetaValue variant=F32 idx=8 boxed=true` — bare `F32` resolves to MetaValue, not DType.\n\n\n`tast_to_hir.rs` enum-variant lookup should prefer the variant whose parent enum matches the expected param type at the call site. Currently appears to be first-found-wins. The `inline_var_values` infrastructure for static-inline-var name disambiguation is a structural analogue — could extend to enum-variant resolution with the call-site type context.\n\n\nThe session's earlier hypothesis that the SIGSEGV was an iface-dispatch problem is wrong. The iface-to-iface cast + vtable registry + fat-ptr rebuild (commits b9f407d, c7a170d, a8cef3c) all work correctly end-to-end:\n- `[iface-cast]` confirmed src=Module(2 methods), tgt=CausalLanguageModel(4 methods)\n- runtime `haxe_iface_fat_ptr_build` returned OK with 4 valid closure slots\n- `model.resetCache()` (slot 3) ran cleanly\n- `model.forwardIds(ids)` (slot 2) entered LlamaModel.forwardIds and progressed through every block\n\nRelated: [[bugs-iface-to-iface-cast-pass-through]] (iface infrastructure now complete).\n\n---\nArchived from Claude memory `bugs_dtype_enum_cross_file_pointer` on 2026-10-18. A record of past work; open items in it may have their own issues.","files":null}]}